  "title": "Crossing knots separated by one port are 2-sums",
  "subject": "How a crossing knot carries its constraint across a three-edge cut when a single port suffices",
  "conclusion": "In two knot spaces glued along a three-edge cut, a crossing knot whose excluded pattern one port separates is the elimination, through that port, of its near part plus the port and its far part plus the port, or is tie-equivalent to a one-sided circuit. The proof uses only complement symmetry and minimality, and it covers 33,556 of the 58,875 crossing knots tested.",
